MODE      cm-threads-i64-ft
SUBJECT   thread.new-indirect whose canon declares ft = (i64) -> () while its table holds an
          (i32) -> () function — the shape #969 found Burroughs accepting

WASM-TOOLS VALIDATE (--features all)
  error: start function must take a single `i32` argument (currently) (at offset 0x6d)
  exit 1 — INVALID

WASMTIME (-W component-model-threading=y -W component-model-async=y)
  Error: failed to parse WebAssembly module
  Caused by:
      start function must take a single `i32` argument (currently) (at offset 0x6d)
  exit 1 — refused at parse, before anything runs

BURROUGHS, before #969
  accepted; run returned 2 — the defect

BURROUGHS, after #969
  refused at load under ErrUnsupportedForm, quoting the same constraint

WHAT THE REFERENCE IMPLEMENTATION SAYS, for completeness
  definitions.py's canon_thread_new_indirect asserts ft is (i32)->() or (i64)->() and then
  trap_if(f.t != ft): in the spec implementation the i64 form is valid and a mismatch TRAPS. The
  toolchains are stricter today and refuse ANY i64 ft at validation — "(currently)" — and this repo
  measures against the toolchains, so the right answer here is a refusal at load, not a trap.

